# Keep the build context to source only. Everything here is either rebuilt
# inside the image, machine-local state, or must never reach a layer.

# Dependency trees — reinstalled from the lockfiles during the build
**/node_modules
**/.venv

# Build output — the image builds its own
frontend/dist
**/*.egg-info
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]

# Local state and secrets
# `**/`, not bare: a bare pattern here is anchored at the context root, so `.env`
# would exclude only /.env — while the Dockerfile's `COPY backend/ ./` and
# backend/README.md's `cp .env.example .env` together produce backend/.env, which
# would then be baked into the image and live-read by config.py's env_file at
# /app/.env. Reads like .gitignore, where a bare pattern DOES match at any depth;
# that mismatch is what hid this (INSPECT-0175).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3
backend/data
backend/logs

# VCS, editors, OS
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
**/.DS_Store

# Docs and meta — not needed to build or run. The one exception is the baseline rule catalogue: it is data the
# evidence report reads at request time (#472), and it lives in docs/ because a register restated in prose
# drifts from the register the code runs.
docs
!docs/baseline-rules.yml
LICENSE
README.md
**/*.md
!backend/README.md
